# Option names and wording derived from carrefinho/prospector-zmk-module (MIT) —
# see NOTICE. Changed: options for features this module does not have are
# dropped, including the ambient light sensor.

config FOCUS_DONGLE_ROTATE_DISPLAY_180
    bool "Rotate the display 180 degrees"
    default n

config FOCUS_DONGLE_LAYER_NAME_UPPERCASE
    bool "Draw layer names in upper case"
    default y
    help
      The keymap's display-name is shown as written when this is off. The
      uppercasing is ASCII-only by construction: bytes above 0x7F belong to a
      UTF-8 sequence and are left alone, so a name in a script with no case is
      unaffected either way.

config FOCUS_DONGLE_FIXED_BRIGHTNESS
    int "Display brightness at boot"
    default 60
    range 1 100
    help
      Where the backlight starts. A screen-brightness binding steps it from
      there at runtime; nothing is persisted, so a power cycle comes back
      here.

      There is no auto-brightness: the Prospector's ambient light sensor is an
      optional breakout rather than a populated part, and this module has never
      had one to test against.
